"Qira felt the waystone flare at dawn on the day Nala came, and knows something crossed there."
"Qira has met one outlander before, forty years ago on the coast, and knows the signs."
"The pictograms tell of a door in the hills where people came from elsewhere, long ago."
"The waystone ring and the caves sit on one thread of gray mana running under the ridge."
"Qira would teach a pupil who could feel mana, and has wanted one for twenty years."
